codex
A broader boundary check exposed an additional, independent defect in `solution.py` itself: whole-string `s.swapcase()` is context-sensitive for Greek final sigma, while the trusted canonical and prompt operate character-by-character. For example, canonical `solve("ΟΣ")` is `"οσ"`, but the candidate returns `"ος"`. I’m updating the preserved differential corpus to include that branch boundary; this reinforces the failure independently of the K semantics.
